20,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Complaints about leaning bikes are common, but the neighboring block found that charging for spaces caused some residents to stop attending meetings.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's true! The same people have had the best spots for five years. Also, daily riders said they'd actually prefer to pay for a spot.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It's a mess. People are shifting other bikes to get out, and the spots past the downpipe get soaked in the rain.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our account is nearly empty, and the ward park is expensive with a long waiting list. We can't rely on outside options.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Adding billing would increase the treasurer's workload. Also, those fancy double-tier racks require significant physical effort and regular maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, if the workload is the issue, perhaps a simple lottery is better than a paid system?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But the daily riders want to pay! If we just do a lottery, the people who need bikes most might lose out.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,A lottery doesn't fix the leaning bikes or the rain. We need a structural change to how we park.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, structural changes cost money we don't have. A paid system would at least fund the building.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the treasurer is already spending hours on small collections. More billing might be the breaking point for the volunteer.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if we prioritize daily riders through payment, we risk the social friction I saw in the neighboring block.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I don't want people fighting, but the current ""first-come, first-served"" for five years is also unfair.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we move to shared racks, we eliminate ""assigned"" spots and the rain issue, but @Toshio mentioned they are hard to use.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. High-maintenance racks are a nightmare. A paid allocation is the most rational way to manage demand.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree that the racks are impractical. Between the effort to lift bikes and the greasing, it's too much.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have to balance fairness, social harmony, and effort. A lottery is the cleanest, but maybe too random.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm torn. I want fairness, but I don't want our neighbors to stop talking to each other.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"If we can't do racks, we're just choosing how to distribute the ""bad"" spots.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's see the options. I suspect the financial incentive will be the most efficient.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I'll support whatever requires the least amount of ongoing administrative failure.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is paid, B is a lottery, and C is shared racks. Given the neighbor block's issues, I'm wary of A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option A sounds fair to the daily riders, but Option B is the most ""equal"" for everyone.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C solves the ""my spot"" argument, but as Toshio said, the hardware is a pain to use.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is out. Option A generates revenue and filters for those who actually need the space.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is a bureaucratic burden. Option B is a once-a-year event. B is much more sustainable.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, I agree. A lottery avoids the resentment of ""buying"" a spot and the workload of billing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,But what about the people who really need it for work? A lottery is just luck.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,Luck is fairer than the current five-year stagnation Yumi found in the minutes.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, luck is not ""fair,"" it's just random. Paid allocation is the only logical way to value the resource.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Logic doesn't matter if the person managing the money quits. I'm voting for the lottery.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I'll vote for the lottery. It's the safest bet for our community's atmosphere.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I still feel for the daily riders, but maybe a yearly reset is better than the current stagnation.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I can't support the racks, and I don't like the idea of paying for a spot in my own home. Lottery it is.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,You're all choosing the path of least resistance over the path of efficiency. I'll stick with Paid Allocation.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Efficiency is useless if it's not sustainable.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems we have a consensus forming around the lottery.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll go with the lottery too. It's the most cheerful way to handle it.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Fine. Enjoy your randomness.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
